# What NOT to ship in the .vsix.
#
# The published extension is just the bundle, the icon, and the docs: esbuild
# has already inlined every dependency into dist/extension.js, so shipping
# sources or node_modules would only bloat the download.
#
# Worth being deliberate here — everything listed in the package is world-
# readable once published.

# Sources and build inputs (dist/ is the shipped artifact).
src/**
out/**
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
node_modules/**

# Build and lint config.
esbuild.mjs
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.eslintrc.json
**/*.map

# Repo scaffolding.
.gitignore
.github/**
*.vsix
scripts/**

# Lockfile: meaningless to consumers, and it enumerates the dependency tree.
package-lock.json
